# tracks_px.sample.jsonl - AMENDMENT A1 pixel-space track fixture (owner A shape).\nSynthetic scene on the fixtures/calibration.json camera, 25 fps, 1280x720.\n\n  track 1  car         northbound on x=12.0 at 6.5 m/s\n  track 2  motorcycle  eastbound on y=22.0, braking 5.5 -> 3.5 m/s at the\n           crossing, arriving ~0.6 s after track 1 clears it\n  track 3  car         following track 1 by 16 m at the same speed\n  track 4  bus         westbound on y=8.0, timed to pass clear of everything\n\nBounding boxes carry +/-1.5 px of jitter, so the least-squares velocity fit\nin edge/calibration/project.py has something real to smooth.\n\nProjected and run through the engine this yields two events: one conflict\n(tracks 1+2) and one severe (tracks 2+3). It is what lets owner B build the\nentire conflict engine before owner A's detector produces a single frame.
